---
// How STUN, ICE, and an optional TURN relay relate to the routers between two browsers.
---
<figure class="architecture-diagram ice-routes">
<div class="diagram-head"><h3>Finding a route between two routers</h3><span>Example addresses</span></div>
<div class="diagram-canvas" role="region" aria-label="Scrollable route diagram" tabindex="0"><svg viewBox="0 0 640 340" role="img" aria-labelledby="ice-routes-title ice-routes-desc"><title id="ice-routes-title">STUN reveals public addresses; ICE checks which route answers</title><desc id="ice-routes-desc">The host browser and guest phone each sit behind a router. Each browser knows its local address and asks a STUN server what address it sees, learning the public address its router presents. ICE checks candidate pairs between the two browsers. In this example one route is blocked by a router and another answers, becoming the direct route. A TURN relay that could carry traffic between the routers is shown dashed because PlayKit does not deploy one.</desc>
<defs><marker id="ice-blue" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="8" refY="5" markerWidth="5" markerHeight="5" orient="auto-start-reverse"><path d="M0 0L10 5L0 10" fill="#315f91"/></marker><marker id="ice-green" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="8" refY="5" markerWidth="5" markerHeight="5" orient="auto-start-reverse"><path d="M0 0L10 5L0 10" fill="#527544"/></marker></defs>
<rect class="node" x="240" y="14" width="160" height="48" rx="10"/><text x="320" y="35" text-anchor="middle">STUN server</text><text class="small" x="320" y="52" text-anchor="middle">Reports the address it sees</text>
<path class="signal" d="M44 194V38H232" marker-end="url(#ice-blue)" marker-start="url(#ice-blue)"/><path class="signal" d="M596 194V38H408" marker-end="url(#ice-blue)" marker-start="url(#ice-blue)"/>
<text class="small" x="54" y="94">What address</text><text class="small" x="54" y="108">do you see?</text><text class="small" x="586" y="94" text-anchor="end">What address</text><text class="small" x="586" y="108" text-anchor="end">do you see?</text>
<path class="data" d="M192 254V118H448V254" marker-end="url(#ice-green)" marker-start="url(#ice-green)"/><text x="320" y="108" text-anchor="middle" style="fill:#527544">A pair that answers becomes the route</text>
<path class="blocked" d="M208 254V152H432V186"/><path class="blocked-mark" d="M424 172L440 188M440 172L424 188"/><text class="small" x="320" y="144" text-anchor="middle">A pair a router blocks</text>
<rect class="router" x="30" y="196" width="190" height="18" rx="4"/><text class="small router-label" x="125" y="209" text-anchor="middle">Router / NAT</text><rect class="router" x="420" y="196" width="190" height="18" rx="4"/><text class="small router-label" x="515" y="209" text-anchor="middle">Router / NAT</text>
<rect class="address" x="54" y="164" width="124" height="22" rx="11"/><text class="small address-text" x="116" y="179" text-anchor="middle">seen as 203.0.113.7</text><rect class="address" x="462" y="164" width="124" height="22" rx="11"/><text class="small address-text" x="524" y="179" text-anchor="middle">seen as 198.51.100.4</text>
<rect class="node" x="30" y="256" width="190" height="64" rx="10"/><text x="125" y="281" text-anchor="middle">Host browser</text><text class="small" x="125" y="302" text-anchor="middle">local 192.168.1.20</text><rect class="node" x="420" y="256" width="190" height="64" rx="10"/><text x="515" y="281" text-anchor="middle">Guest phone</text><text class="small" x="515" y="302" text-anchor="middle">local 10.0.0.8</text>
<path class="optional" d="M220 205H282V262M420 205H358V262"/><rect x="250" y="262" width="140" height="48" rx="8" fill="#e7e1f4"/><text x="320" y="283" text-anchor="middle">TURN relay</text><text class="small" x="320" y="300" text-anchor="middle">Not deployed in PlayKit</text>
</svg></div><figcaption>STUN shows each browser how its router presents it to the internet. ICE then checks pairs of candidates and keeps one that answers. Which route wins depends on the networks, and without a TURN relay some pairs of networks have no route at all.</figcaption><div class="legend"><span><i></i>STUN discovery</span><span><i class="game"></i>Working route</span><span><i class="blocked-key"></i>Blocked check</span><span><i class="relay"></i>Relay, not deployed</span></div></figure>
